# Verification bar

Follow `docs/sdlc.md`. The worker who posts the verdict did not write the code. A green CI run is not a verdict, and a separate approving review is not the merge gate.

`python3 scripts/check_sdlc_gates.py` already fails proprietary DLLs, high-confidence secrets, a dropped GPL-3.0 root license, skill lint, Rust tests, and `mkdocs build --strict`. Read the diff for what those commands cannot see.

Block the pull request only when one of these is true at the current head:

- A required run fails (`scripts/check_sdlc_gates.py`, offline evals, or staged drills).
- A user would hit a bug this pull request introduces or newly reaches.
- A doc line this pull request added or edited is wrong.

Anything else is a `PASS+NOTES` note or a follow-up. A problem already on `main` does not block unless this pull request copies it or newly reaches it. Record the verdict on the pull request with the full head SHA (`PASS`, `PASS+NOTES`, or `FAIL`). A new head needs a new verdict.

When `/poteto-mode` is installed, this bar is the one in `autopilot-full` and `shipping`. Do not invent poteto flags.
